E","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in 4.5.stable\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.5.stable - Windows 10 - Vulkan / d3d12  (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce GTX 1060 6GB (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.6636) - Intel(R) Core(TM) i5-8400 CPU @ 2.80GHz (6 threads) - 15.91 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nSetting the color of an instance uniform with source_color results in a, roughly, 30% darker color than expected vs a global uniform when using Forward+ with either Vulkan or d3d12. Compatibility works as expected.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Create 2 color rects\n2. Create a shader that alters the fragment COLOR using a uniform source_color, duplicate it and change it to instance uniform in the copy.\n3. Attach each shader to a shader material and attach both to their respective color rects using a script.\n4. Set the shader parameter on the material with set_shader_parameter on the color rect with the global uniform to for example: grey #808080\n5. Set the instance parameter with CanvasItem.set_instance_shader_parameter on the color rect with the instance uniform to the same #808080\n6. Run the project and note that the rect with instance uniform is roughly 30% darker than expected, looking closer to  something like #383838\n\nLeft rect: uniform  - Right rect: instance uniform\n<img width=\"642\" height=\"639\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e17c75fb-7a21-49c2-89ee-3e4d3deffc78\" />\n\n\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nhttps://github.com/Pinedal/shaderparameter_bugtest","closed_by":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html